Photosynthesis is the process plants use to convert sunlight into energy. Inside plant cells, chlorophyll in chloroplasts absorbs sunlight and uses that energy to split water molecules into oxygen and hydrogen. The oxygen is released into the air, while the hydrogen combines with carbon dioxide from the atmosphere to form glucose, which the plant stores as energy. In simple terms, sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide are turned into food and oxygen.
